---
/**
 * `Vytápění`   the third section of /ubytovani.
 *
 * COPY IS THE OLD SITE'S, VERBATIM. It reads like a page out of a boiler
 * manual, and it stays that way: every clause in it answers a real question a
 * group arriving in February has, and the person who wrote it knew the building.
 * Not our copy to smooth out.
 *
 * DESIGN: the page's ONE dark band. Two full-bleed splits in a row would flatten
 * out, and this is the natural place to break them   it is the only section on
 * the page with no photograph to go with it (there is no picture of a pellet
 * boiler, and there should not be one). So the section becomes the break itself:
 * `--les` ground, `--omitka` type, no image, short measure.
 *
 * That also gives the page the shape the homepage has   light, light, dark,
 * light   instead of an unbroken run of alternating pale bands.
 *
 * ⚠ `--omitka` on `--les` is 15.45:1, the site's default inverse pairing. The
 * heading must NOT be `--mosaz`: brass on the dark ground is 3.00:1 and fails
 * for text (docs/02-design-system.md §1.2). On dark, brass type is
 * `--mosaz-svetla`   used below for the icon and the link only.
 */
import IconLucide from '../../IconLucide.astro';
import HermanekSprig from '../../decor/HermanekSprig.astro';
---

<section id="vytapeni" class="section vytapeni" aria-labelledby="vytapeni-nadpis">
  {/*
    ⚠ THE ONE PLACE ON THIS PAGE WHERE THE LINE WORK IS WHITE.

    docs/02-design-system.md §4 rule 5 lists exactly three grounds for white
    line: over photography, in the two maps, and over `--les`. This band is
    `--les`, so this is the sanctioned case   and it is also the only band on
    the page with no photograph, which is what left its right-hand two thirds
    empty. The plant fills it with the site's own drawing language rather than
    with a stock texture or a gradient.

    Rule 3 keeps it unfilled: this is a big outline drawing, not a watermark
    shape. It is held well back at 0.16 so it reads as ground behind the type
    rather than as a second thing competing with it   measured, not guessed:
    at 0.16 over --les it is about the same value as the hairline rules
    elsewhere on the page, and the body copy above it keeps its full 12.91:1.
  */}
  <HermanekSprig class="vytapeni-rostlina" />

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="vytapeni-inner" data-reveal="up">
      <IconLucide name="flame" size={34} class="vytapeni-ikona" />

      <h2 id="vytapeni-nadpis">Vytápění</h2>

      <p>
        Vytápění objektu zajišťuje peletkový kotel, dále krbová vložka, kde palivo
        je dřevo v&nbsp;kombinaci s&nbsp;akumulační nádrží nahřívanou elektrickými
        spirálami. Je možné topit jen krbem, od&nbsp;kterého jsou horkovzdušné
        rozvody do&nbsp;horních ložnic, nebo využít komfortu kombinace peletkového
        kotle a&nbsp;el.&nbsp;vytápění akumulační nádrží, popřípadě oba režimy
        kombinovat.
      </p>

      {/*
        The electricity is metered and billed by actual consumption, which is
        the first thing anyone reading a heating section wants to know next.
        A link, not a repeat of the rate   the rate lives in src/data/cenik.ts
        and is printed on one page only.
      */}
      <p class="vytapeni-pozn">
        <a href="/terminy-a-ceny" class="link-more link-on-dark">
          <span>Elektřina se účtuje podle skutečné spotřeby</span>
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .vytapeni {
    position: relative;
    background-color: var(--color-les);
    color: var(--color-omitka);
    /* The sprig is drawn past the band's edges and must be cut off by them. */
    overflow: hidden;
    /* `position: relative` alone is not enough   the copy has to win the stack
       even though it comes later in source order but has no z-index of its own. */
    isolation: isolate;
  }

  .vytapeni-rostlina {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: -1;
    /*
     * Anchored to the band's right edge and allowed to run off it top and
     * bottom. A decorative mark that fits neatly inside its box reads as a
     * sticker; one that is cropped reads as something the page is standing on.
     */
    top: -12%;
    inset-inline-end: -2rem;
    width: auto;
    height: 124%;
    color: var(--color-omitka);
    opacity: 0.16;
  }

  /*
   * Hidden below 64rem, and not just scaled down. On a phone the copy runs the
   * full width of the band, so the drawing would sit directly behind the
   * paragraph rather than beside it   and a 0.16 line under body text is
   * exactly the sort of thing that survives review on a desktop and makes the
   * page look dirty on the device most of these readers actually use.
   */
  @media (width < 64rem) {
    .vytapeni-rostlina {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  .vytapeni-inner {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .vytapeni-ikona {
    /* --mosaz-svetla on --les = 6.19:1. Plain --mosaz would be 3.00:1. */
    color: var(--color-mosaz-svetla);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-omitka);
  }

  p {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    /* --kamen on --les = 12.91:1. Stone, not frost   --jinovatka is reserved
       for winter content (docs/02-design-system.md §1.3), and a heating
       section is the most tempting wrong place to reach for it. */
    color: var(--color-kamen);
  }

  .vytapeni-pozn {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: var(--text-body);
  }
</style>
